/*
 * 86Box    A hypervisor and IBM PC system emulator that specializes in
 *          running old operating systems and software designed for IBM
 *          PC systems and compatibles from 1981 through fairly recent
 *          system designs based on the PCI bus.
 *
 *          This file is part of the 86Box distribution.
 *
 *          Hardware text font for the PGC core.
 *
 *          The card holds this face as a stroke font rather than a
 *          bitmap: a pointer table into short programs whose high nibble
 *          steps a pen one unit across the cell and whose low nibble
 *          names the ink shape drawn at the new position. Every program
 *          visits a cell at most once, so the face fits one shape per
 *          cell: a 7 by 9 figure with descenders, in the 8 by 12 cell the
 *          IBM Options and Adapters Technical Reference describes.
 *
 *          One row per scanline, top first; each cell is a nibble, the
 *          leftmost cell in the top nibble, 0 for no ink.
 *
 * Authors: skiretic
 *
 *          Copyright 2026 skiretic.
 */
